<spell-notebook "popup theming">
	<header level="1">
		Popup
		<header>A popup displays additional information on top of a page.</>
	</>
	<popup-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
			<item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
			<item link="#themes">Themes</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Theme with the public `--ui-popup-*` tokens: set one on the element, on any ancestor (`:root` for every popup),
			or on the box through `::part(popup)`. They inherit into the shadow root, where the sheet reads each through a
			private alias, so nothing inside blocks them. `wide` and `very wide` swap the max width for
			`--ui-popup-wide-width` / `--ui-popup-very-wide-width`; a slotted header reads `--ui-popup-header-font-size`
			from the popup. The CSS-only tooltip reads `--ui-tooltip-*` tokens on the element that carries it.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			/* every popup on the page */
			:root {
			  --ui-popup-radius: 0.5em;
			}
			/* one kind */
			ui-popup.help {
			  --ui-popup-max-width: 320px;
			  --ui-popup-distance: 0.75em;
			}
			/* the CSS-only tooltips */
			[data-tooltip] {
			  --ui-tooltip-distance: 0.75em;
			}
			```
		</>
		<message state="info" size="small">
			<markdown>
				The host resets the colour remap and `--ui-scale`, so a popup opened from inside a red message or a large
				button is neither red nor large: give the popup its own `color` / `size`. Never set the `--_ui-popup-*` names:
				they're the sheet's private plumbing.
			</>
		</>
		<markdown>Edit a value below to try it.</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-popup" playground>
				<ui-button icon="plus" aria-label="Add users"></>
				<ui-popup label="Add users to your feed"></>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			The theme menu above picks the theme for every page of the site:  Spell, Glass, Fruity or Merlot,
			each restyling this component through its tokens.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
